* ''The words, the flow unblurred'' (operator, 2026-11-18: //"Approve all five, keep lei per house, retire the flag."//; lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/flow-unblur #/ruled): unlock opens custody and `lares wear N` chooses the face, asking no route, the pūlama's lent set bounding it; `vessel seed` becomes `vessel lay`, so seed names the genesis offer alone; oracle names the divination sigil alone, the floor's read-face taking W26's owed name, floor, and the stored genesis island reading as the founding record, never written after founding; carry names nothing after the burn, `carry-parity`, `carry.ts` and the bundle manifest taking the names of the keep's restore and the census drill (rank 13b); every route prompt names whose route it asks (the vessel's, face hN's, or the pūlama's); the keep lei stands one per house, strung by the steward. The dev-install flag retires with no exception in its place: no house carves anything out (the ruling on workspaces and read-back by descent (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions #/ruled-workspaces)). Lares-Awakens' proposals, talked out and taken (open to the operator's overturn): pin names the floor alone, the rotatable wiki pins reading as holds and the genesis seed pin as the seed witness; keep names the backup alone, D2's undo reading as a revert; two floor types in code, `ReleaseFloor` (steward-sealed, on the board) and `LocalFloor` (one house's adopt, a receipt, its base release); the 2 a.m. test asks of every operator-facing string which word a tired operator misreads during a rite. The build rides rank 4i.

